      "writtenOn": "2024-01-31T17:33:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t have the cycles to grok if this would be a problem, but FYI regarding:\n\n\u003e To my knowledge, Skia does not have any platform specific helpers\nfor Vulkan, so we only need to expose a general \"ganesh_vulkan\"\nbackend for clients to use.\n\nThere are helper methods for working with `AHardwareBuffer`s on Android that are guarded by `SK_BUILD_FOR_ANDROID`, which is set when building to run _on_ Android, not just _in_ the Android framework. Could this be a problem for Bazel customers what might want to embed Skia into an Android app using Vulkan, or could they still set that define?\n\n(See `include/android/GrAHardwareBufferUtils.h` for an example, but `SK_BUILD_FOR_ANDROID` is checked elsewhere for Vulkan stuff too.)",
      "revId": "12d3f9ee7350481598ecae1cdbf6a5e63cef7285",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
